cards:
- id: first-agent-task
  title: "Example: let an agent close its first ticket"
  description: |
    1. `barkcli intake "Fix the flaky login test"` — classify into a card+spec.
    2. `barkcli run "fix the flaky login test" --yes` — the autonomy loop
       plans, spawns an agent in a worktree, and merges only if the
       acceptance gate passes.
    3. Watch it live: `barkcli serve` → Orchestrate → /api/run/live.
  column: todo
  priority: high
  labels: [onboarding]
  checklist:
  - text: "pick a backend (opencode / claude / codex) or set BARKCLI_AGENT_CMD"
    done: false
  - text: "run the loop on a small, safe task first"
    done: false
  - text: "read the report: attempts, gate result, merged branch"
    done: false
  - text: "let it rip: --agents 3 for the parallel pool"
    done: false
  comments: []
  attachments: []
  pinned: true
  version: 1
  created_at: 2026-10-24T00:00:00Z
  updated_at: 2026-10-24T00:00:00Z
- id: define-review-policy
  title: Decide what human review means for agent PRs
  description: |
    The runner can auto-merge gate-passing work (--yes) or leave branches
    ready-unmerged for a human. Write down which task classes need eyes and
    encode it in the dispatch policy — then hold agents to it.
  column: review
  priority: medium
  labels: [policy]
  checklist: []
  comments: []
  attachments: []
  pinned: false
  version: 1
  created_at: 2026-10-24T00:00:00Z
  updated_at: 2026-10-24T00:00:00Z
